# core=3.8: cascade:PatientReported, the provenance individual core had been
#     missing. Added to BOTH hardcoded provenance sets in this package, which is
#     the whole of the work: the ProvenanceType union in src/models/common.ts
#     and VALID_PROVENANCE_TYPES in src/validator/validator.ts. The second is
#     the one that mattered — a value absent from it is REJECTED at runtime, so
#     bumping only the row would have left this SDK failing a conformant record.
#     No term modelled in this release changes.
#     DISTINCT FROM cascade:SelfReported, and the axis is WHO KEYED IT IN rather
#     than who it came from. Both originate with the patient: SelfReported is
#     the patient entering data directly, while PatientReported is "information
#     originating from the patient's own account and recorded by another party
#     or system (history related to a clinician, imported questionnaire
#     responses)". The intermediary may have summarized, paraphrased or
#     mis-transcribed, so a consumer weighing how directly a claim is attested
#     needs the two kept apart. Neither is a substitute for the other and this
#     SDK maps neither onto the other.
#     The individual is a DIRECT subclass of cascade:DataProvenance, under
#     neither ClinicalGenerated nor ConsumerGenerated, because a patient's
